    "articles": [
      {
        "locale": "zh-Hans",
        "title": "扩展的视界在哪里结束，文明又从哪里开始",
        "summary": "扩展视界不是地图上最远能够到达的位置，而是一个运行仍能稳定读取、协调、承载、修复并承担责任的现实范围。技术、制度与跨载体结构可以不断把视界推远，但每一次扩展都会把边界迁移到新的信息、协调、资源、时间、意义与治理问题。当跨世代知识、制度、基础设施、陌生人协作与共同未来开始彼此耦合时，问题便从“还能扩大多少”进入“是否已经接近文明阈值”。",
        "href": "/articles/book4-article-037",
        "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-037-ZH-HANS-ARTICLE"
      },
      {
        "locale": "en",
        "title": "Where the Horizon of Expansion Ends—and Civilization Begins",
        "summary": "The horizon of expansion is not the farthest place a runtime can reach on a map. It is the range of reality the runtime can still read, coordinate, carry, repair, and take responsibility for with stability. Technology, institutions, and cross-carrier structures can keep pushing this horizon outward, but each expansion moves the boundary into new problems of information, coordination, resources, time, meaning, and governance. When transgenerational knowledge, institutions, infrastructure, cooperation among strangers, and a shared future become coupled, the question shifts from “how much larger can this get?” to “has the runtime approached a civilization threshold?”",
        "href": "/articles/book4-article-037",
        "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-037-EN-ARTICLE"
      }
    ],
